# Repo-root .dockerignore — applied to every `docker build ... .` from
# this directory. The two runtime Dockerfiles
# (plugins/smai-compute-localgpu/dockerfiles/runtime{,-cpu}.Dockerfile)
# COPY packages/smai-core/ and packages/smai-runtime/ into the image
# (Round 19); without an ignore the daemon receives the whole repo
# (~hundreds of MB) as build context on every rebuild.
#
# This is an exclude-list, not an allowlist. The Dockerfiles only COPY
# the two paths they need, so anything not COPY-referenced is dropped
# from the image regardless of what's in context; this file's job is
# purely to keep the *sent* context small (and incidentally to keep
# bind-mounted dev-machine cruft from invalidating the build cache).

# Python build/runtime cruft
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches (lots of small files, churn the cache for no reason)
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright/
.hypothesis/

# Git + GitHub (the CI workflow ships outside the image)
.git/
.github/

# Frontend assets — the runtime images do not serve the SPA
node_modules/
apps/ui/dist/
apps/ui/.turbo/
apps/ui/.tanstack/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Tests. The runtime images run `python -m smai_runtime.runner` and
# the locked experiment.py template; they do not run pytest. The
# tests/ trees under each package + the top-level tests/ would
# otherwise be carried inside the COPY-ed package sources (per-package
# trees) or as a wasted top-level send. The per-package
# `tests/_<task>_<purpose>.py` fakes also import sibling-plugin paths
# that aren't installed in the image, which would just be dead weight.
tests/
**/tests/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Local Claude Code workspace state
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Runtime artifacts written by `smai dev` etc.
.smai/

# uv lock (the image installs from the package pyproject.toml, not the
# workspace lock — and the lock changes on every `uv lock` regardless of
# whether anything the runtime image cares about moved)
uv.lock

# smai-ui staged SPA bundle (build artifact, never relevant to runtime)
packages/smai-ui/src/smai_ui/static_spa/
